<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Gibraltar</h1><p class="st-meta">1713 CE – present · capital Gibraltar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A British territory on the rock at the entrance to the Mediterranean, held since 1704 and still claimed by Spain.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>An Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fleet under Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-rooke">George Rooke</a> captured Gibraltar in 1704 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>, nominally for the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a> claimant Charles. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> ceded the town and fortress to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a> in perpetuity by Article X of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-utrecht">Treaty of Utrecht</a> in 1713.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Gibraltar became a fortress and naval base guarding the Strait, surviving the Great Siege of 1779-1783 and serving as a key base in the Napoleonic and World Wars. Its mixed population of Genoese, Spanish, Maltese, Jewish and British origin developed a distinct identity and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llanito">Llanito</a> speech. It became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-colony">Crown colony</a> in 1830.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> pressed its claim at the UN; Gibraltarians voted to stay British in 1967, and Spain closed the land border from 1969 to 1985. In 2002 they rejected shared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>. Today it is a self-governing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-overseas-territories">British Overseas Territory</a>, with its border regime negotiated after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brexit">Brexit</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/gibraltar.jpg" alt="Gibraltar" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Created on behalf of Isabella I of Castile in 1502; this version uploaded by Denelson83 (talk · contribs) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Gibraltar.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1713 CE – present</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gibraltar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>George Eliott, Joshua Hassan, Peter Caruana</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>United Kingdom</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>British Gibraltar</dd></dl></aside></div>
